=== layout: section

# Effects of Inbreeding

=== layout: one-panel

# *Nonrandom Mating*

@body

- Nonrandom mating includes
  - *Consanguineous mating* &#8211; mating between genetically related individuals
  - *Assortative mating* &#8211; mating between individuals with similar phenotypes
- Consanguineous mating reduces the frequency of heterozygotes and increase the frequency of homozygotes compared to the Hardy-Weinberg genotype frequencies.

=== layout: one-panel

# *INBREEDING*

@body

- Mating between relatives such as first cousins &#8211; frequency of heterozygotes gets smaller than it is with random mating.
- Start with self fertilization of Aa plant\:
  - After first generation &#8211; &#188; AA, &#189; Aa, &#188; aa
    - it reduces proportion of heterozygous\: &#189;
  - After second generation\: &#189; &#215; &#189;  = 1/4
  - After third generation\: &#189; &#215; &#189; &#215; &#189;  = 1/8
  - So on&#8230;
- This section we measure the reduction in quantitative terms.

=== layout: one-panel

# *Effects of Inbreeding*

@body

- Most genetic diseases are caused by recessive alleles.
- Inbreeding is harmful, and much  of the effect is due to rare recessive alleles that would not otherwise become homozygous.
- Inbreeding increases the probability of forming recessive genotype.
  - Among Caucasians, albinism 1 in 20,000 among offspring of non-relatives vs. 1&#160;in 2000 among relative offspring

=== layout: two-panels

# *Blue Fugates of Kentucky*

@left

![Slide image 4](assets/lect15e-inbreeding/image_004.png)

@right

- Fugates family lived in the hills of Kentucky
  - commonly known as the "Blue Fugates" or the Blue People
- Carriers of recessive disease methemo-globinemia, which gives sufferers blue-tinged skin
- Due to remote area where they lived, there was a very high level of consanguinity in marriage between families.

=== layout: one-panel

# *Inbreeding increases the chance of having progeny that are homozygous for a rare recessive trait*

@body

![Slide image 5](assets/lect15e-inbreeding/inbreeding_recessive_frequency.plot.svg)

=== layout: one-panel

# *Effect of Inbreeding*

@body

- The frequencies of the two homozygotes have increased and the frequency of the heterozygotes has decreased compared to the Hardy-Weinberg frequency.
  - For each genotype, the change in frequency is directly proportional to the [inbreeding coefficient, F]{color=#CC00CC}.
- For a completely inbred population, F&#160;=&#160;1.
  - The frequency of genotype AA will be p, the frequency of Aa will be 0, and the frequency of genotype aa will be q.

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

# *The frequency of heterozygotes is reduced as inbreeding increases*

@body

- Heterozygosity (H1) Graph is given by
  - H1 = 2pq (1-F)
- F = 0 random mating
- F = 1  no heterozygous remaining in the population

![Slide image 6](assets/lect15e-inbreeding/image_006.png)

- Inbreeding reduces the frequency of heterozygous genotypes, relative to random mating, and increases the frequency of homozygous genotypes.

=== layout: section

# Inbreeding Coefficient

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

# *Inbreeding Coefficient*

@body

- Inbreeding coefficient\:  It is a measure of genetic effects of inbreeding, symbolized by letter  &#8220;F&#8221;
- Proportionate reduction in heterozygosity (H1) in an inbred organism  compared with the heterozygosity expected with random mating.
  - F = (2pq &#8211; H1)/2pq
    - F = 0 (no inbreeding)
    - F = 1 (complete inbreeding) ??
  - H1 = 2pq (1-F)
- So genotypic frequencies in inbred population\:
  - AA\: p^2^ (1-F) + pF
  - Aa\: 2pq (1-F)
  - aa\: q^2^ (1-F) + qF

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme


@body

- The effects of consanguineous mating can be quantified using the inbreeding coefficient, F.
- Frequency with Genotype 	Consanguineous Mating
  - AA\: p^2^ + pqF
  - Aa\: 2pq &#8211; 2pqF
  - aa\: q^2^ + pqF

=== layout: one-panel

@body

[The]{color=#40458C} [*inbreeding coefficient of individual*]{color=#40458C} [is the probability that the individual carries alleles that are identical by descent.]{color=#40458C}

=== layout: two-panels

# *Inbreeding Coefficient*

@left

- Proportionate reduction in heterozygosity (H1) in an inbred organism  compared with the heterozygosity expected with random mating.
  - F = (2pq &#8211; H1)/2pq
    - F = 0 (no inbreeding)
    - F = 1 (complete inbreeding)
  - H1 = 2pq (1-F)

@right

{table-style=working padding="2pt 4pt" column-widths="3.2,1.4,1.4,1.4"}
|  | [AA]{text-align=center} | [Aa]{text-align=center} | [aa]{text-align=center} |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| [F (general)]{vertical-align=middle} | [p^2^ (1-F) + pF]{text-align=center vertical-align=middle} | [2pq (1-F)]{text-align=center vertical-align=middle} | [q^2^ (1-F) + qF]{text-align=center vertical-align=middle} |
| [F=0 (no inbreeding)]{vertical-align=middle} | [p^2^]{text-align=center vertical-align=middle} | [2pq]{text-align=center vertical-align=middle} | [q^2^]{text-align=center vertical-align=middle} |
| [F=1 (complete inbreeding)]{vertical-align=middle} | [p]{text-align=center vertical-align=middle} | [0]{text-align=center vertical-align=middle} | [q]{text-align=center vertical-align=middle} |

