=== layout: one-panel

# *Is it legal to marry your first cousin in Illinois?*

@body

- In Illinois, first cousins cannot legally marry unless\:
  - both parties are 50 or older,
  - or a licensed physician certifies that either one of the parties is &#8220;permanently and irreversibly sterile.&#8221;
- This certification must be filed when applying for a marriage license.
- Read more at\: [https\://www.bnd.com/news/state/illinois/article284904242.html](https://www.bnd.com/news/state/illinois/article284904242.html)
- [https\://www.ilga.gov/legislation/publicacts/fulltext.asp?Name=098-0597](https://www.ilga.gov/legislation/publicacts/fulltext.asp?Name=098-0597)

